Let the Marlin int8-activation path (VLLM_MARLIN_INPUT_DTYPE=int8, the launchers'
INT8_ACT=int8) accept zero-point int4 weights.

compressed-tensors W4A16_ASYM exports (llm-compressor AWQ with symmetric=false) carry a
weight_zero_point per group and load as scalar_types.uint4. The Marlin kernel set already
instantiates that pairing with int8 activations (csrc/.../marlin/generate_kernels.py,
"AWQ-INT4 with INT8 activation", kS8 x kU4, covered by
tests/kernels/quantization/test_marlin_gemm.py), and the wrapper already permutes the zero
points with is_a_8bit -- but two asserts written to refuse W8A8 only admit uint4b8, so such
a checkpoint dies at process_weights_after_loading the moment INT8_ACT is set:

  AssertionError: W8A8 is not supported by marlin kernel.

The asserts now admit uint4 next to uint4b8; 8-bit weights stay refused. Measured on a
random asymmetric int4 g128 weight at this model's shapes (bench/test_marlin_int8_asym.py,
RTX 3090): W4A8-int8 relative error 0.9-1.05% against the float reference, the W4A16 path
0.26% -- the int8 activation noise alone, the same as on a symmetric body.

Apply from the installed vllm package directory:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/marlin-int8-asym-zp.patch

Validated against vLLM 0.28.0; the same two hunks apply to 0.29.0 at an offset.

--- cut by hand against pristine v0.28.0 with patches/series applied, line numbers exact (not a cpuchip/vllm topic commit yet; import it there and re-export) ---

--- a/model_executor/kernels/linear/mixed_precision/marlin.py
+++ b/model_executor/kernels/linear/mixed_precision/marlin.py
@@ -143,7 +143,10 @@
         is_a_8bit = c.act_type is not None and c.act_type.itemsize == 1
 
         if is_a_8bit:
-            assert c.weight_type == scalar_types.uint4b8, (
+            # syv patch (marlin-int8-asym-zp): the kernel set instantiates
+            # kS8 x kU4 (AWQ zero-point weights, int8 activations) next to
+            # kS8 x kU4B8; only 8-bit weights have no int8-activation kernel.
+            assert c.weight_type in (scalar_types.uint4b8, scalar_types.uint4), (
                 "W8A8 is not supported by marlin kernel."
             )
 
--- a/model_executor/layers/quantization/utils/marlin_utils.py
+++ b/model_executor/layers/quantization/utils/marlin_utils.py
@@ -738,7 +738,9 @@
 
     a_scales = None
     if input_dtype == torch.int8:
-        assert wtype == scalar_types.uint4b8, (
+        # syv patch (marlin-int8-asym-zp): uint4 (zero-point) weights have an
+        # int8-activation kernel too; only 8-bit weights do not.
+        assert wtype in (scalar_types.uint4b8, scalar_types.uint4), (
             "W8A8-INT8 is not supported by marlin kernel."
         )
         reshaped_x, a_scales = marlin_quant_input(reshaped_x, input_dtype)
